    "selection_reason": "Freeze six previously unused Canon-EF-or-EF-S seller snapshots spanning an 18-55mm kit form, two low-cost primes, a renewed third-party 35mm premium prime, a Canon 35mm L prime, and a Canon 24-70mm L zoom; eleven unused lens and optics pages covering the kit and 50mm model families, prime-lens scope, optical design, coatings, chromatic and spherical aberration, vignetting, flare, optical transfer, and diffraction; and three unused single-post community examples involving a normal lens plus tracker, a newly acquired macro lens, and a 55-250mm moon image. Seller prices, ratings, condition words, bundles, coatings, sharpness, autofocus, stabilization, and performance language remain frozen assertions rather than current offers or controlled comparisons. Different focal lengths, apertures, mounts, conditions, subject distances, processing, displays, print sizes, and shooting tasks cannot be collapsed into a universal price-to-sharpness curve. The set supports an output-normalized, task-matched, reversible lens trial and a lowest-cost passing decision gate; it does not prove that expensive glass always wins, that a kit lens is always sufficient, or that a single community image establishes a lens cutoff. All exact URLs used by existing formal cases and contemporaneous Q53-Q55 reservations were excluded, and the set was reserved against the concurrent Q57-Q58 pipelines before capture.",
